<title>UK: GOLF-LEADING WORLD RANKINGS.</title>
<headline>GOLF-LEADING WORLD RANKINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Steve Jones has entered</p>
<p>the top 20 in the world rankings list for the first time after</p>
<p>his victory in the Phoenix Open at the weekend.</p>
<p>Top 20 (U.S. unless stated)</p>
<p> 1. Greg Norman (Australia)	11.18  points average</p>
<p> 2. Tom Lehman			  9.96</p>
<p> 3. Colin Montgomerie (Britain)   9.07</p>
<p> 4. Ernie Els (South Africa)	8.95</p>
<p> 5. Nick Faldo (Britain)	    7.93</p>
<p> 6. Masashi Ozaki (Japan)	   7.58</p>
<p> 7. Davis Love III		    7.56</p>
<p> 8. Fred Couples			7.30</p>
<p> 9. Mark O'Meara			6.94</p>
<p> 10. Corey Pavin			6.80</p>
<p> 11. Phil Mickelson		   6.76</p>
<p> 12. Nick Price (Zimbabwe)	  6.28</p>
<p> 13. Steve Stricker		   6.23</p>
<p> 14. Scott Hoch			 5.69</p>
<p> 15. Mark McNulty (Zimbabwe)	5.63</p>
<p> 16. Steve Elington (Australia)   5.52</p>
<p> 17. Bernhard Langer (Germany)    5.49</p>
<p> 18. Steve Jones			5.37</p>
<p> 19. Tom Watson			 5.25</p>
<p> 20. David Duval			5.15</p>
